data.content:
The `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 package upgraded from **OpenAPI.NET v1 to v2** (`Microsoft.OpenApi` 2.x). Here are the breaking changes in your code:

## Key Changes

1. **`OpenApiAny` types removed** — `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. are gone. Use native `JsonNode` instead.

2. **`OpenApiSecurityScheme` no longer used as dictionary key** — `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` changed from `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>` to a simpler model.

3. **`Nullable` property removed from schema** — OpenAPI v3.1 uses `type: ["string", "null"]` instead of `nullable: true`.

4. **`OpenApiResponse` → keyed differently** — `Responses` is now a dictionary of `OpenApiResponse` but construction is the same (this part likely still works).

5. **`OpenApiReference` changed** — `Type` is now a string-based `ReferenceType`.

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // JsonNode replaces OpenApiString/OpenApiAny
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference
        {
            Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme,
            Id = "oauth2"
        }
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Replace .Nullable with type array manipulation
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

## Summary of fixes

| Old (v1) | New (v2) |
|----------|----------|
| `new OpenApiString("1.0")` | `JsonValue.Create("1.0")` |
| `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `using System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
| `property.Value.Nullable = false` | `property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null` |

The `ReferenceType` enum and `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` dictionary pattern remain similar in shape, but if you get errors on `ReferenceType`, ensure you're using `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.ReferenceType` (now string constants in some builds — check your exact package version).
